  lessonId: contentVocab
  lessonTitle: Content Vocabulary
  lessonImage: {fileID: 0}
  lessonDesc: "    Force - A push and pull that can cause an object to change its
    speed, direction, and shape.\n    Contact Force - Forces that are equal in strength
    and opposite in direction, resulting in no net force on an object.\n    Non-Contact
    Force - Forces that act on an object without physical contact, such as gravity
    or magnetism.\n    Balanced Force - Forces that act on an object through direct
    physical contact, such as friction or normal force."
